<section>
  <p class="kicker"><%= link_to_page "guides", label_type: :nav, class: "cta" %></p>
  <h1>Use the Go&rsquo;s pad and button</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Cycle through pages with the pad. Open menus with the button. Use the diagnostic pages at the workbench.
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="feature">
    <div>
      <h3 id="two-contacts">The pad moves, <span class="highlight">the button acts</span>.</h3>
      <p>
        The capacitive touch pad on the top edge cycles through the four pages,
        without changing settings. The button on the side opens the current page&rsquo;s menu,
        and each further press changes the value in the selected row.
      </p>
      <p>
        Two pages have a menu. All the settings you can change with the controls are in the radar menu,
        the first screen used to set up the device. Each press applies the change immediately,
        except clearing the ADS-B address, which asks you to confirm on a second screen.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="shot">
      <%= screen_image_tag "menu-radar.png", alt: "The settings menu: light, aircraft, FLARM, units, range, plot and alarm, with the button's key CHANGE and the pad's key NEXT at the foot" %>
      <figcaption>The radar menu</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <div class="feature feature--reverse">
    <div>
      <p>The last row in <span class="mono">SETTINGS</span>, <span class="mono">POWER</span>, picks what switches the Go on and off. Tap the pad to move down the rows. The menu slides up one line at <span class="mono">BRAVO</span> and another at <span class="mono">POWER</span>. See <%= link_to_page "power", label: "how cable mode works", anchor: "cable-mode" %>.</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="shot">
      <%= screen_image_tag "menu-power.png", alt: "SETTINGS with the last row selected: POWER reads BUTTON" %>
      <figcaption>The radar menu with its last row in view</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <ul class="points">
    <li>Tap the pad to go to the next page</li>
    <li>Touch the pad for a second to silence an active alarm, or return to the radar if no alarm is active</li>
    <li>Press the button to open the menu, if the page has one</li>
    <li>Press again to change the value in the selected row</li>
    <li>In the menu, tap the pad after the last row to return to the page</li>
    <li>Leave the controls untouched for a minute to return to the page automatically</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="feature feature--reverse">
    <div>
      <h3 id="callsign">Your callsign, <span class="highlight">entered with two controls</span>.</h3>
      <p>
        <span class="mono">CALLSIGN</span> is the only row that opens an entry field
        instead of changing a value. Inside it, the controls swap roles:
        the pad changes the character above the bar, and the button moves to the
        next character. The cycle runs from a blank to a dash, <span class="mono">A</span> to
        <span class="mono">Z</span>, <span class="mono">0</span> to
        <span class="mono">9</span>, then back to the blank. If you pass a letter,
        keep cycling to reach it again with the same gesture.
      </p>
      <p>
        Press the button on the last character to save the callsign. Any blanks
        at the end are removed. To clear a callsign, change the first
        character to a blank and press the button. The button label
        reads <span class="mono">ERASE</span> when the first character is blank. If you leave the field before finishing or leave it untouched for a minute, nothing is saved.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="shot">
      <%= screen_image_tag "menu-callsign.png", alt: "The callsign field: S-BLIP at triple height, a bar under the third character, and the keys NEXT for the button and CHANGE for the pad" %>
      <figcaption>The callsign field</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <div class="shots">
    <figure class="shot">
      <%= screen_image_tag "menu-callsign-blank.png", alt: "The callsign field with a blank as the first character, the bar under it, and the button's key now reading ERASE" %>
      <figcaption>The first character blanked</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="shot">
      <%= screen_image_tag "menu-callsign-none.png", alt: "The aircraft menu after the press, with the CALLSIGN row selected and reading NONE" %>
      <figcaption>The callsign is cleared</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <div class="feature feature--reverse">
    <div>
      <h3 id="diagnostics">Four pages to cycle through, <span class="highlight">diagnostics to open by name</span>.</h3>
      <p>
        Tap the pad to cycle through the radar, the list, the instruments and the g-meter. Other pages stay outside this cycle, so you do not end up on the satellite bars while changing pages in flight. On a device with no inertial sensor, tapping skips the g-meter page rather than showing
        <span class="mono">NO SENSOR</span> every fourth time.
      </p>
      <p>
        Open the diagnostic pages by name from the list&rsquo;s menu. When you close them, you return to the page you were on. The screens below are for checks at the workbench, on the apron and for bug reports. You cannot reach them by cycling through pages with the pad. The Bravo log shows the software running on a paired skyBlip Bravo, its battery status and what its receiver receives. To record a flight for a bug report or a discharge test, open the device page in the briefing app and start the recording. The device screen shows what will be erased. Press the button to confirm and begin recording.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="shot">
      <%= screen_image_tag "menu-nearby.png", alt: "The nearby menu: status, satellites, radio log, Bravo log and self test, the five pages opened by name" %>
      <figcaption>The list&rsquo;s menu</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <div class="shots">
    <figure class="shot">
      <%= screen_image_tag "status.png", alt: "The status page: position fix and satellites, position, track, traffic count, transmit state, the sensor hub, pressure, the two altitudes, speed, vertical speed, and the battery in volts and percent" %>
      <figcaption>Status</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="shot">
      <%= screen_image_tag "satellites.png", alt: "The satellites page: one bar per satellite grouped by constellation, with a dotted reference line at 40 dB-Hz" %>
      <figcaption>Satellites</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="shot">
      <%= screen_image_tag "radio-log.png", alt: "The radio log: below the position fix, the pulse-per-second (PPS) signal state and the background noise level, one row per short radio transmission received or sent, newest first, with its time, direction, channel, contents, address and signal level" %>
      <figcaption>Radio log</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="shot">
      <%= screen_image_tag "self-test.png", alt: "The self test page: RADIO SX1262 CCA OK shows the radio listening before transmission, GNSS L76K 2 HZ shows the GPS receiver calculating two positions per second, and each board component has its test result" %>
      <figcaption>Self test</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Gesture</th><th>On a page</th><th>In a menu</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th>Tap the pad</th>
          <td>goes to the next page, or rejects a confirmation request on the screen</td>
          <td>moves to the next row, or returns to the menu&rsquo;s page after the last row</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>Touch the pad, 1&nbsp;s</th>
          <td>silences an active alarm, or returns to the radar if no alarm is active</td>
          <td>returns to the radar</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>One press of the button</th>
          <td>opens this page&rsquo;s menu, or accepts a confirmation request on the screen</td>
          <td>acts on the selected row, with each further press changing its value again</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>Hold the button, 2&nbsp;s</th>
          <td colspan="2">switches the device off</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>The same hold, finger on the pad</th>
          <td colspan="2">switches it off and leaves the screen blank, for storage</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

